  "description": "Profile and optimize mid-range logical buffer operations on the Ryzen 9 5900X, retaining the requirement that adoption materially improves real workloads.\n\n## Background\n\nBuffers of 8-64 words can be dominated by dispatch and call overhead as well as instruction throughput. The relevant production consumers are row operations, parity generation and dense matrix work. Measure actual consumers before selecting unrolling, zero-copy access, fusion or memory-traffic changes; do not infer performance from the AVX2 label.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- [hard] REQ-01: Publish profiles and baseline measurements for 8-64-word logical operations and their production consumers, with neighboring smaller/larger sizes and boundary/unaligned cases. Freeze exact operations, inputs, cache regimes, statistical rules and primary consumer cells before optimization.\n\n- [hard] REQ-02: Compare candidate unroll factors, dispatch hoisting, zero-copy BitSlice use and measured useful fusions against the established kernels. Adopt only when the family's predeclared confidence-bound worthwhile-effect and complexity rules demonstrate real consumer benefit and its equivalence-margin non-regression rule passes. Allow repeatable smaller gains when justified by that frozen rule; preserve no-win outcomes.\n\n- [hard] REQ-03: Compare equivalent XOR/parity operations against ISA-L and consuming dense-matrix work against M4RI. Match input representation and operation semantics and include all adapter, setup, conversion and output costs; distinguish isolated throughput from consumer benefit.\n\n- [hard] REQ-04: Preserve exact logical semantics, canonical bit indexing and zero tail padding in the shared suites. Keep the one canonical buffer/dispatch abstraction and route measured decisions through existing tuning mechanisms.\n\n- [hard] REQ-05: Commit annotated release assembly and profiles explaining dispatch overhead, memory traffic, spills, dependence limits or bandwidth saturation. Produce reviewed worker-sized implementation leaves if the measured story needs several independent changes.\n\n- [hard] REQ-06: Satisfy the [Zen 3 measurement contract](dev/active/1a379447-zen3-cpu-performance/measurement-contract.md) for correctness, reproducible release benchmarks, comparison validity and adoption; receipts pin its committed version, the frozen protocol and the cell addendum. Include mandatory before/after evidence for production changes and preserve negative outcomes.\n\n## Notes\n\nUse family-specific effect thresholds justified before confirmation. This story has no fixed 15% adoption hurdle and does not widen its scope beyond mid-range logical-buffer consumers.\n\n\n\nSource references: [IsaL2026], [AlbrechtBard2026].",
